  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Nitration is an electrophilic aromatic substitution reaction. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect increases the rate of nitration whereas the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect decreases the rate of nitration.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>Br</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>but</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>dominant</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/416dfc6e-e7a4-4fcc-85d3-22a4ab1c5c88-image.png\" style=\"width: 456px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is strongly deactivating</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>Br</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math> deactivating</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math> activating group</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
